;; Camera image on real hardware. Checked in as a deliberately failing fixture.
;;
;; It composes cleanly and fails `silt check --buildroot`: libcamera has
;; `depends on !BR2_STATIC_LIBS` and profile:minimal sets static libs. That
;; conflict lives in Buildroot's Kconfig, not in any fragment, so compose alone
;; cannot see it — which is the whole reason the verifier exists.
;;
;; `silt solve` on this must produce solve/testdata/edge-camera.expected, and
;; that file is asserted by TestEdgeCameraExplanation. Explanation quality is
;; the subjective part of this project and therefore the part most likely to
;; rot quietly; pinning the output is the only guard against that.
;;
;; The target was target:rpi4-64, hand-written and never built. silt fixpoint
;; found kbuild dropping its BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_INTREE_DTS_NAME, so it is gone
;; and this composes the imported target:raspberrypi4-64 instead. That target
;; states no kernel options: the Pi 4 defconfig builds a vendor kernel from
;; BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_DEFCONFIG="bcm2711", which brings its own.

(image edge-camera

  (compose
    target:raspberrypi4-64
    profile:minimal
    feature:networking
    feature:wifi
    feature:camera)

  (repair-policy
    (minimize changed-symbols)
    (keep target)))
